{"id":154897021,"slug":"pharmacy-benefit-managers-hiked-generic","title":"Pharmacy Benefit Managers Hiked Generic Drug Costs by $7.3b","subtitle":"In case you wanted to understand how stupid big health is, it's this stupid.","post_date":"2025-01-16T04:06:30.570Z","audience":"everyone","type":"newsletter","canonical_url":"https://thefrontierpsychiatrists.substack.com/p/pharmacy-benefit-managers-hiked-generic","wordcount":434,"source":"api","fetched_at":"2026-09-13T21:49:28.835Z","body_sha256":"e55cd6758815a2a96dd750469f45da230f38ec20143733891ecc0ac12de040cf","text_words":447,"complete":true,"body_html":"<p>The Frontier Psychiatrist is a newsletter. And that means sometimes we’re writing about the <em>news</em>. Today's news?  A new report from the Federal Trade Commission.  I've previously written,<a href=\"https://open.substack.com/pub/thefrontierpsychiatrists/p/sopranorx-the-pbm-mafia-revisited?r=1ct8f&amp;utm_campaign=post&amp;utm_medium=web&amp;showWelcomeOnShare=false\"> in excruciating detail</a>, about how the wholly-owned subsidiaries of Big Health companies that manage contracted rates around pharmaceuticals are running a <em>racket</em>.  I mean that in a very literal sense of the term, as in racketeering.  As in extortion.  <em>Your money or (drugs that save) your life.  </em>Here is one prior story in which I highlight how bonkers this system is—this time, for generics.</p><p class=\"button-wrapper\" data-attrs=\"{&quot;url&quot;:&quot;https://thefrontierpsychiatrists.substack.com/subscribe?&quot;,&quot;text&quot;:&quot;Subscribe now&quot;,&quot;action&quot;:null,&quot;class&quot;:null}\" data-component-name=\"ButtonCreateButton\"><a class=\"button primary\" href=\"https://thefrontierpsychiatrists.substack.com/subscribe?\"><span>Subscribe now</span></a></p><div class=\"digest-post-embed\" data-attrs=\"{&quot;nodeId&quot;:&quot;1277473e-0ea0-47b1-b375-c882ce11626d&quot;,&quot;caption&quot;:&quot;Welcome to the Frontier Psychiatrists, a newsletter about health. Also, I have a full-length album released today. It’s called Perfect is the Enemy of the Good. It’s available on Spotify! Follow it, and I won’t be upset if you “listen to it” on repeat when you leave the house for the weekend. This is a joke.&quot;,&quot;cta&quot;:null,&quot;showBylines&quot;:true,&quot;showDescription&quot;:true,&quot;showImage&quot;:true,&quot;size&quot;:&quot;sm&quot;,&quot;isEditorNode&quot;:true,&quot;title&quot;:&quot;\\&quot;How is that possible?!\\&quot;&quot;,&quot;publishedBylines&quot;:[{&quot;id&quot;:2277375,&quot;name&quot;:&quot;Owen Scott Muir, M.D&quot;,&quot;bio&quot;:&quot;Dr. Owen Scott Muir is a healthcare innovator and entrepreneur, working across innovative care, payment models, technology, regulatory compliance, and education. He's a graduate of Amherst College.&quot;,&quot;photo_url&quot;:&quot;https://substackcdn.com/image/fetch/f_auto,q_auto:good,fl_progressive:steep/https%3A%2F%2Fbucketeer-e05bbc84-baa3-437e-9518-adb32be77984.s3.amazonaws.com%2Fpublic%2Fimages%2F1c03f44d-4506-4843-989f-0d38e66c6946_400x400.jpeg&quot;,&quot;is_guest&quot;:false,&quot;bestseller_tier&quot;:100}],&quot;post_date&quot;:&quot;2023-10-11T14:39:37.801Z&quot;,&quot;cover_image&quot;:&quot;https://i.scdn.co/image/ab67616d0000b273581ea01af9dfd3ebd24693ad&quot;,&quot;cover_image_alt&quot;:null,&quot;canonical_url&quot;:&quot;https://thefrontierpsychiatrists.substack.com/p/how-is-that-possible&quot;,&quot;section_name&quot;:null,&quot;video_upload_id&quot;:null,&quot;id&quot;:137807460,&quot;type&quot;:&quot;newsletter&quot;,&quot;reaction_count&quot;:10,&quot;comment_count&quot;:2,&quot;publication_id&quot;:null,&quot;publication_name&quot;:&quot;The Frontier Psychiatrists &quot;,&quot;publication_logo_url&quot;:&quot;https://substackcdn.com/image/fetch/f_auto,q_auto:good,fl_progressive:steep/https%3A%2F%2Fbucketeer-e05bbc84-baa3-437e-9518-adb32be77984.s3.amazonaws.com%2Fpublic%2Fimages%2F997b8496-9b4d-43c2-b393-6f8a77945b00_1080x1080.png&quot;,&quot;belowTheFold&quot;:false,&quot;youtube_url&quot;:null,&quot;show_links&quot;:null,&quot;feed_url&quot;:null}\"></div><p>PBMs are a remarkable scam. At its height, among the most storied criminal enterprises in recent memory, <a href=\"https://open.substack.com/pub/thefrontierpsychiatrists/p/escobar-health-reimagining-cocaine?r=1ct8f&amp;utm_campaign=post&amp;utm_medium=web&amp;showWelcomeOnShare=false\">Pablo Escobar’s coke cartel</a> (that is a link to a prior parody, “joinEscobar.health”) was making about $4 billion a year in annual revenue.</p><div class=\"captioned-image-container\"><figure><a class=\"image-link image2 is-viewable-img\" target=\"_blank\" href=\"https://substackcdn.com/image/fetch/$s_!ryyA!,f_auto,q_auto:good,fl_progressive:steep/https%3A%2F%2Fsubstack-post-media.s3.amazonaws.com%2Fpublic%2Fimages%2Fc158e60d-c493-478f-a4cc-e264284c5b95_1456x971.png\" data-component-name=\"Image2ToDOM\"><div class=\"image2-inset\"><picture><source type=\"image/webp\" srcset=\"https://substackcdn.com/image/fetch/$s_!ryyA!,w_424,c_limit,f_webp,q_auto:good,fl_progressive:steep/https%3A%2F%2Fsubstack-post-media.s3.amazonaws.com%2Fpublic%2Fimages%2Fc158e60d-c493-478f-a4cc-e264284c5b95_1456x971.png 424w, https://substackcdn.com/image/fetch/$s_!ryyA!,w_848,c_limit,f_webp,q_auto:good,fl_progressive:steep/https%3A%2F%2Fsubstack-post-media.s3.amazonaws.com%2Fpublic%2Fimages%2Fc158e60d-c493-478f-a4cc-e264284c5b95_1456x971.png 848w, https://substackcdn.com/image/fetch/$s_!ryyA!,w_1272,c_limit,f_webp,q_auto:good,fl_progressive:steep/https%3A%2F%2Fsubstack-post-media.s3.amazonaws.com%2Fpublic%2Fimages%2Fc158e60d-c493-478f-a4cc-e264284c5b95_1456x971.png 1272w, https://substackcdn.com/image/fetch/$s_!ryyA!,w_1456,c_limit,f_webp,q_auto:good,fl_progressive:steep/https%3A%2F%2Fsubstack-post-media.s3.amazonaws.com%2Fpublic%2Fimages%2Fc158e60d-c493-478f-a4cc-e264284c5b95_1456x971.png 1456w\" sizes=\"100vw\"><img src=\"https://substackcdn.com/image/fetch/$s_!ryyA!,w_1456,c_limit,f_auto,q_auto:good,fl_progressive:steep/https%3A%2F%2Fsubstack-post-media.s3.amazonaws.com%2Fpublic%2Fimages%2Fc158e60d-c493-478f-a4cc-e264284c5b95_1456x971.png\" width=\"509\" height=\"339.4498626373626\" data-attrs=\"{&quot;src&quot;:&quot;https://substack-post-media.s3.amazonaws.com/public/images/c158e60d-c493-478f-a4cc-e264284c5b95_1456x971.png&quot;,&quot;srcNoWatermark&quot;:null,&quot;fullscreen&quot;:null,&quot;imageSize&quot;:null,&quot;height&quot;:971,&quot;width&quot;:1456,&quot;resizeWidth&quot;:509,&quot;bytes&quot;:1493005,&quot;alt&quot;:null,&quot;title&quot;:null,&quot;type&quot;:&quot;image/png&quot;,&quot;href&quot;:null,&quot;belowTheFold&quot;:false,&quot;topImage&quot;:true,&quot;internalRedirect&quot;:null,&quot;isProcessing&quot;:false,&quot;align&quot;:null,&quot;offset&quot;:false}\" class=\"sizing-normal\" alt=\"\" srcset=\"https://substackcdn.com/image/fetch/$s_!ryyA!,w_424,c_limit,f_auto,q_auto:good,fl_progressive:steep/https%3A%2F%2Fsubstack-post-media.s3.amazonaws.com%2Fpublic%2Fimages%2Fc158e60d-c493-478f-a4cc-e264284c5b95_1456x971.png 424w, https://substackcdn.com/image/fetch/$s_!ryyA!,w_848,c_limit,f_auto,q_auto:good,fl_progressive:steep/https%3A%2F%2Fsubstack-post-media.s3.amazonaws.com%2Fpublic%2Fimages%2Fc158e60d-c493-478f-a4cc-e264284c5b95_1456x971.png 848w, https://substackcdn.com/image/fetch/$s_!ryyA!,w_1272,c_limit,f_auto,q_auto:good,fl_progressive:steep/https%3A%2F%2Fsubstack-post-media.s3.amazonaws.com%2Fpublic%2Fimages%2Fc158e60d-c493-478f-a4cc-e264284c5b95_1456x971.png 1272w, https://substackcdn.com/image/fetch/$s_!ryyA!,w_1456,c_limit,f_auto,q_auto:good,fl_progressive:steep/https%3A%2F%2Fsubstack-post-media.s3.amazonaws.com%2Fpublic%2Fimages%2Fc158e60d-c493-478f-a4cc-e264284c5b95_1456x971.png 1456w\" sizes=\"100vw\" fetchpriority=\"high\"></picture><div class=\"image-link-expand\"><div class=\"pencraft pc-display-flex pc-gap-8 pc-reset\"><button tabindex=\"0\" type=\"button\" class=\"pencraft pc-reset pencraft icon-container restack-image\"><svg aria-hidden=\"true\" width=\"20\" height=\"20\" viewBox=\"0 0 20 20\" fill=\"none\" stroke-width=\"1.5\" stroke=\"var(--color-fg-primary)\" stroke-linecap=\"round\" stroke-linejoin=\"round\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\"><g><path d=\"M2.53001 7.81595C3.49179 4.73911 6.43281 2.5 9.91173 2.5C13.1684 2.5 15.9537 4.46214 17.0852 7.23684L17.6179 8.67647M17.6179 8.67647L18.5002 4.26471M17.6179 8.67647L13.6473 6.91176M17.4995 12.1841C16.5378 15.2609 13.5967 17.5 10.1178 17.5C6.86118 17.5 4.07589 15.5379 2.94432 12.7632L2.41165 11.3235M2.41165 11.3235L1.5293 15.7353M2.41165 11.3235L6.38224 13.0882\"></path></g></svg></button><button tabindex=\"0\" type=\"button\" class=\"pencraft pc-reset pencraft icon-container view-image\"><svg xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" width=\"20\" height=\"20\" viewBox=\"0 0 24 24\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"2\" stroke-linecap=\"round\" stroke-linejoin=\"round\" class=\"lucide lucide-maximize2 lucide-maximize-2\"><polyline points=\"15 3 21 3 21 9\"></polyline><polyline points=\"9 21 3 21 3 15\"></polyline><line x1=\"21\" x2=\"14\" y1=\"3\" y2=\"10\"></line><line x1=\"3\" x2=\"10\" y1=\"21\" y2=\"14\"></line></svg></button></div></div></div></a><figcaption class=\"image-caption\">Get in the game, with Escobar Health</figcaption></figure></div><p>According to the Federal Trade Commission, the companies that your insurance company owns that they have negotiations with around how much drugs cost?  In addition to making on the order of $485 billion a year last year in top line revenue, also inflated generic drug prices by $7.3 billion.</p><p>They didn't even have to run a tank at the Supreme Court.  What a deal!  This is not the only scam, this is just <a href=\"https://www.beckershospitalreview.com/pharmacy/ftc-finds-top-3-pbms-inflated-drug-prices-by-7-3b.html?origin=BHRE&amp;utm_source=BHRE&amp;utm_medium=email&amp;utm_content=newsletter\">on </a><em><a href=\"https://www.beckershospitalreview.com/pharmacy/ftc-finds-top-3-pbms-inflated-drug-prices-by-7-3b.html?origin=BHRE&amp;utm_source=BHRE&amp;utm_medium=email&amp;utm_content=newsletter\">generic</a></em><a href=\"https://www.beckershospitalreview.com/pharmacy/ftc-finds-top-3-pbms-inflated-drug-prices-by-7-3b.html?origin=BHRE&amp;utm_source=BHRE&amp;utm_medium=email&amp;utm_content=newsletter\"> drug prices:</a></p><blockquote><p>CVS Caremark, Cigna's Express Scripts and UnitedHealth's Optum Rx — marked up specialty generic drug prices, generating over $7.3 billion in excessive revenues from 2017 to 2022.</p></blockquote><p>Ouch.  It just gets more stupid from here.  And I can get into the detail on it, and usually I would, but I just took a redeye back from San Francisco, and I'm here to tell you, this is not a good deal.</p><p>It's not a good deal for any of us.  It's especially a bad deal if you're the federal government. All those federal employees?  They have a health plan.  If I was in an incoming administration, that had already demonstrated some hostility towards Pharmacy Benefit Managers, and <a href=\"https://www.washingtonexaminer.com/news/white-house/3286986/musk-expected-operate-doge-white-house-complex-close-access-trump/\">I</a> was trying to slash expenses?  </p><p>Well don't you know, someone might decide to yank the safe harbor that makes this otherwise completely illegal activity completely legal, and then just let the chips fall they may?</p><p>I don't know. It's not up to me.  But if I had been that<a href=\"https://open.substack.com/pub/thefrontierpsychiatrists/p/dont-lie-to-congress-advice-to-the?r=1ct8f&amp;utm_campaign=post&amp;utm_medium=web&amp;showWelcomeOnShare=false\"> chief executive officer of a PBM subsidiary of a major payer who has been accused of lying to Congress</a>, I might be a little less comfortable today than I was the prior day.</p><p>Then again, I might just be a little obsessed with insurance.  Like that Dorothy, in my podcast adaptation and parody of the Wizard of Oz:</p><div class=\"digest-post-embed\" data-attrs=\"{&quot;nodeId&quot;:&quot;131a881f-d1ae-4f80-abb8-2fdb85899873&quot;,&quot;caption&quot;:&quot;The Frontier Psychiatrists is a daily enough health-themed publication. It’s also a podcast. Sometimes, I need a break from serious coverage of policy. In those cases, I amuse myself with David Foster Wallace-esque fan fiction about health policy, like this first chapter in my Wizard of Oz-themed parody about health insurance. Dorothy gets strep…then psoriasis…then OCD! Join us for a little health-themed absurdity, and maybe, just maybe, we will all learn something.&quot;,&quot;cta&quot;:null,&quot;showBylines&quot;:true,&quot;showDescription&quot;:true,&quot;showImage&quot;:true,&quot;size&quot;:&quot;md&quot;,&quot;isEditorNode&quot;:true,&quot;title&quot;:&quot;The Wizard Of Odds, Ch 1&quot;,&quot;publishedBylines&quot;:[{&quot;id&quot;:2277375,&quot;name&quot;:&quot;Owen Scott Muir, M.D&quot;,&quot;bio&quot;:&quot;Dr. Owen Scott Muir is a healthcare innovator and entrepreneur, working across innovative care, payment models, technology, regulatory compliance, and education. He's a graduate of Amherst College.&quot;,&quot;photo_url&quot;:&quot;https://substackcdn.com/image/fetch/f_auto,q_auto:good,fl_progressive:steep/https%3A%2F%2Fbucketeer-e05bbc84-baa3-437e-9518-adb32be77984.s3.amazonaws.com%2Fpublic%2Fimages%2F1c03f44d-4506-4843-989f-0d38e66c6946_400x400.jpeg&quot;,&quot;is_guest&quot;:false,&quot;bestseller_tier&quot;:100}],&quot;post_date&quot;:&quot;2024-08-29T12:53:28.412Z&quot;,&quot;cover_image&quot;:&quot;https://substack-post-media.s3.amazonaws.com/public/images/edfe1cef-5498-44dc-aa8f-0f49f5c17c9b_3000x2000.jpeg&quot;,&quot;cover_image_alt&quot;:null,&quot;canonical_url&quot;:&quot;https://thefrontierpsychiatrists.substack.com/p/the-wizard-of-odds-ch-1&quot;,&quot;section_name&quot;:null,&quot;video_upload_id&quot;:null,&quot;id&quot;:148263251,&quot;type&quot;:&quot;podcast&quot;,&quot;reaction_count&quot;:1,&quot;comment_count&quot;:0,&quot;publication_id&quot;:null,&quot;publication_name&quot;:&quot;The Frontier Psychiatrists &quot;,&quot;publication_logo_url&quot;:&quot;https://substackcdn.com/image/fetch/f_auto,q_auto:good,fl_progressive:steep/https%3A%2F%2Fbucketeer-e05bbc84-baa3-437e-9518-adb32be77984.s3.amazonaws.com%2Fpublic%2Fimages%2F997b8496-9b4d-43c2-b393-6f8a77945b00_1080x1080.png&quot;,&quot;belowTheFold&quot;:true,&quot;youtube_url&quot;:null,&quot;show_links&quot;:null,&quot;feed_url&quot;:null}\"></div><p class=\"button-wrapper\" data-attrs=\"{&quot;url&quot;:&quot;https://thefrontierpsychiatrists.substack.com/p/pharmacy-benefit-managers-hiked-generic?utm_source=substack&utm_medium=email&utm_content=share&action=share&quot;,&quot;text&quot;:&quot;Share&quot;,&quot;action&quot;:null,&quot;class&quot;:null}\" data-component-name=\"ButtonCreateButton\"><a class=\"button primary\" href=\"https://thefrontierpsychiatrists.substack.com/p/pharmacy-benefit-managers-hiked-generic?utm_source=substack&utm_medium=email&utm_content=share&action=share\"><span>Share</span></a></p><p></p><p></p><p></p>","text":"The Frontier Psychiatrist is a newsletter. And that means sometimes we’re writing about the news . Today's news? A new report from the Federal Trade Commission. I've previously written, in excruciating detail , about how the wholly-owned subsidiaries of Big Health companies that manage contracted rates around pharmaceuticals are running a racket . I mean that in a very literal sense of the term, as in racketeering. As in extortion. Your money or (drugs that save) your life. Here is one prior story in which I highlight how bonkers this system is—this time, for generics.\n\nSubscribe now\n\nPBMs are a remarkable scam. At its height, among the most storied criminal enterprises in recent memory, Pablo Escobar’s coke cartel (that is a link to a prior parody, “joinEscobar.health”) was making about $4 billion a year in annual revenue.\n\nGet in the game, with Escobar Health\n\nAccording to the Federal Trade Commission, the companies that your insurance company owns that they have negotiations with around how much drugs cost? In addition to making on the order of $485 billion a year last year in top line revenue, also inflated generic drug prices by $7.3 billion.\n\nThey didn't even have to run a tank at the Supreme Court. What a deal! This is not the only scam, this is just on generic drug prices:\n\nCVS Caremark, Cigna's Express Scripts and UnitedHealth's Optum Rx — marked up specialty generic drug prices, generating over $7.3 billion in excessive revenues from 2017 to 2022.\n\nOuch. It just gets more stupid from here. And I can get into the detail on it, and usually I would, but I just took a redeye back from San Francisco, and I'm here to tell you, this is not a good deal.\n\nIt's not a good deal for any of us. It's especially a bad deal if you're the federal government. All those federal employees? They have a health plan. If I was in an incoming administration, that had already demonstrated some hostility towards Pharmacy Benefit Managers, and I was trying to slash expenses?\n\nWell don't you know, someone might decide to yank the safe harbor that makes this otherwise completely illegal activity completely legal, and then just let the chips fall they may?\n\nI don't know. It's not up to me. But if I had been that chief executive officer of a PBM subsidiary of a major payer who has been accused of lying to Congress , I might be a little less comfortable today than I was the prior day.\n\nThen again, I might just be a little obsessed with insurance. Like that Dorothy, in my podcast adaptation and parody of the Wizard of Oz:\n\nShare"}